	(symbol (lib_id "power:GND") (at 25.4 27.94 0) (unit 1) (exclude_from_sim no) (in_bom yes) (on_board yes) (dnp no) (uuid "8c958a14-ae25-4929-ab63-ded5a90788a0") (property "Reference" "#PWR027" (at 25.4 22.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))) (property "Value" "GND" (at 25.4 31.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))) (property "Footprint" "" (at 25.4 27.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))) (property "Datasheet" "~" (at 25.4 27.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))) (pin "1" (uuid "0f0dde02-c719-4a4d-9a36-08f29019c828")) (instances (project "car" (path "/ffdedf3a-67e8-4282-b496-2684f4fc429c" (reference "#PWR027") (unit 1)))))
	(text "XIAO pads, USB-C up, from the top: left D0 D1 D2 D3 D4 D5 D6, right 5V GND 3V3 D10 D9 D8 D7;\nBAT+ and BAT- on the back. The microSD of the Sense board takes D8 CLK, D9 DAT0, D10 CMD and\nGPIO21 for DAT3, inside: leave D8-D10 free. D1 is spare, for the optional aux channel." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 193.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "965f0e24-4564-455e-bf85-08c6317fd1d2"))
	(text "Keys: the bench's two buttons (PLAN-ESP32.md 3.1): a 10 k pull-up on D0, OK straight to\nground, NAV through 10 k; 0 V, 1.62 V, and 3.12 V at rest.\nThe IMU is optional (DNP): on the I2C bus with the display, at 0x6A, it needs no GPIO.\nThe GM10 runs from the LM2940's 5 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f831e033-7292-422f-a15d-a28f9a9e83fc"))
	(text "RC inputs, per channel: 10 k in series; a BAT43 to 3V3 that holds a 5 V receiver's pulse\nunder the pin's 3.6 V; 100 k to ground that holds the pin low with the receiver off, as the\nRC inputs wake the chip. A 3.3 V receiver's high reads about 3.0 V, over the 2.48 V needed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 236.22 190.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "629de0a7-3e18-42ff-bbf9-aba4d2bd7e16"))
	(text "Power: never the receiver rail straight into the 5V pad. C1, low ESR, and C2 soak up the\nservo's spikes, and the LM2940 holds 5 V for the 5V pad and the GM10. It is guaranteed from\n6.25 V in; on a 5.9 V BEC its dropout, 0.2 V at most at 100 mA, leaves room, to confirm on\nthe bench. C3 keeps it stable: 22 u or more, ESR 0.1 to 1 ohm: a low-ESR electrolytic, the\nEEU-FR1C101, as small tantalums run over 1 ohm. No diodes (decided 2026-10-24), so the\nUSB is never plugged in while the car or a LiPo powers the board: the two 5 V would meet\non the 5V pad.\nThe LiPo on the BAT pads carries the shutdown when the car is switched off." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "34b517d8-e0c4-4d48-863f-011b80794c71"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))) (embedded_fonts no))
